  "summary": "The motor rotor and the pump impeller are on one shaft inside a fully enclosed pressure boundary. The stator windings are sealed from the pumped liquid by a thin stator liner (can); the rotor is sealed by its own can. A small flow of pumped liquid circulates through the motor gap to remove heat and lubricate the sleeve bearings. There is no shaft seal and no coupling, so leakage paths are eliminated; the motor housing gives secondary containment.",
  "classification": {
    "family": "Rotodynamic (centrifugal), radial flow",
    "configuration": "Sealless, close-coupled canned motor",
    "api_610_type": "Sealless; covered by API 685"
  },
  "model_configuration": {
    "circulation": "Basic front-to-back circulation from discharge (other arrangements: reverse circulation, high-temperature with external cooler, self-venting for volatile liquids)",
    "bearings": "Carbon/graphite journals on SiC sleeves; bearing wear monitor on rear cover",
    "cans": "Hastelloy C / stainless thin-wall liners (typical)"
  },
